WEBVTT

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.579
Finally, the last form of the day.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:40.999
Welcome to Stampytown, population five.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.549
And now for the finishing touch.

00:00:56.974 --> 00:00:59.393
The cycle of bureaucracy.

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:04.064
Sweet gorilla of Manila!
A letter from the Central Bureaucracy.

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:05.566
"Attention, Hermes Conrad.

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:09.653
"You are about to receive a letter
from the Central Bureaucracy."

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:12.573
My God! It's from the Central Bureaucracy!

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:17.119
I'm having a poker game tonight with
some friends from my old cryogenics job.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:18.328
You guys interested?

00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:20.831
I don't know. I only gamble with chumps.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.374
- I'll play.
- I'm in!

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:23.709
Leela, Fry, Robot.

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.753
No matter what it is you're doing tonight,
I'm available.

00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:27.880
We're playing poker.

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:30.632
But I'm warning you
my friends are serious players.

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.259
Bah! Big shots.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.595
I say let the dice do the talking.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.874
Wow, you look happy. Is someone fired?

00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:51.920
Better. The Central Bureaucracy
is conducting an inspection tomorrow.

00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:56.842
I will finally be promoted to Grade 35,
the 35th highest Grade there is.

00:01:58.302 --> 00:02:00.721
Hermes, wait. We're having a poker party.

00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:03.390
Stay and whip off
a batch of your famous jerk dip.

00:02:03.473 --> 00:02:06.518
Sorry. I spent all day
putting my office in order.

00:02:06.602 --> 00:02:09.396
Now I got to go home
and relax the traditional Jamaican way.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:11.565
A glass of warm milk
and a good night's sleep.

00:02:11.648 --> 00:02:15.193
Jamaican? I thought you were
some kind of outer space potato man.

00:02:16.486 --> 00:02:18.363
Ah, that must be my old boss.

00:02:20.198 --> 00:02:23.035
- Hello, Leela. You're fired.
- I know.

00:02:23.118 --> 00:02:26.663
I'm sorry, but it's just that you're over
a year late for work at this point.

00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:28.999
Let the games begin!

00:02:29.499 --> 00:02:34.296
So I told Leela, "Your request for a date
is most flattering, but I must decline.

00:02:34.379 --> 00:02:36.673
"These office romances never work out.

00:02:36.757 --> 00:02:40.052
"After all, that is how
I met my horrible wife."

00:02:41.386 --> 00:02:43.347
That's a good one.

00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:47.017
But you never wore your ring.
I didn't know you had a wife.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.936
And my wife doesn't know I have a job.

00:02:49.019 --> 00:02:51.647
I keep my personal
and professional life separate.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.190
Come on, let's deal.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.901
You'll have plenty of time
to talk when you're poor.

00:02:55.984 --> 00:02:57.277
What's with the specs, Bender?

00:02:57.361 --> 00:02:58.904
They're my lucky shades.

00:02:58.987 --> 00:03:00.822
I stole them off some lucky guy

00:03:00.906 --> 00:03:04.034
while his lucky seeing eye dog
was taking a whiz.

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:05.369
Huh?

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:09.922
Hey!

00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:13.877
I can't spell anything with these cards.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.428
Finally, I have a good claw. See?

00:03:23.462 --> 00:03:27.925
Three human females, a number
and a king giving himself brain surgery.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.220
It doesn't matter
how many human females you have.

00:03:31.303 --> 00:03:32.429
Bender's on a hot streak.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:36.183
Eh, what can I say?
Must be my lucky shades.

00:03:38.852 --> 00:03:40.229
Nothing. Nothing.

00:03:40.312 --> 00:03:42.606
Crap. Crap. Garbage.

00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:45.192
Read 'em and leak saltwater.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.320
My baby's milk money!

00:03:49.863 --> 00:03:50.989
I am broke.

00:03:51.073 --> 00:03:52.950
What will I tell my horrible wife?

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.493
If I were you I'd be more worried

00:03:54.576 --> 00:03:58.038
about that tapeworm
going to town on your intestines.

00:03:59.665 --> 00:04:02.167
Let me see those glasses.

00:04:02.251 --> 00:04:05.796
Um... ah...

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:08.840
Oh, my various gods, X-ray specs!

00:04:09.466 --> 00:04:11.969
Guys, I swear those are prescription.

00:04:12.052 --> 00:04:15.389
I need them for reading stuff...
On the other side of stuff.

00:04:15.472 --> 00:04:17.766
- You cheater.
- Break his neck!

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:20.519
No, don't hurt him. He's my best friend.

00:04:32.281 --> 00:04:36.118
Hey, you wouldn't hit a guy
with X-ray glasses, would you?

00:04:37.369 --> 00:04:38.537
Easy on the arm!

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.081
Oh, my ass!

00:04:41.331 --> 00:04:42.332
Ow!

00:04:55.137 --> 00:04:57.973
Great cow of Moscow!

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.896
Uh... it was ghosts. Big ones.

00:05:04.271 --> 00:05:05.522
And a tornado.

00:05:05.647 --> 00:05:08.859
I'll never pass inspection now.

00:05:08.942 --> 00:05:13.196
They'll bust me lower than a limbo stick
at carnival time.

00:05:13.655 --> 00:05:17.159
And that's as low as limbo sticks get.

00:05:17.242 --> 00:05:20.162
Aw, hey, come on, don't worry.
We'll watch you clean up.

00:05:20.245 --> 00:05:21.371
It's too late.

00:05:21.455 --> 00:05:24.625
The inspector will be here
in exactly one second.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.877
Who the hell are you?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.212
Morgan Proctor, Bureaucrat, Grade 19.

00:05:29.296 --> 00:05:32.215
Hermes Conrad, Bureaucrat, Grade 36.

00:05:34.927 --> 00:05:37.262
Enough friendly banter.
Shall we begin the inspection?

00:05:37.346 --> 00:05:38.889
This way, please.

00:05:39.348 --> 00:05:42.059
Hermes, you seem awfully calm about this.

00:05:42.142 --> 00:05:44.478
Don't worry. I have a plan.

00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:45.938
I'm going to jump!

00:05:46.355 --> 00:05:47.898
No! No!

00:05:48.315 --> 00:05:49.566
Do a flip!

00:05:51.985 --> 00:05:55.405
Don't do it, Hermes!
You have so much to live for!

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.741
I get it. Reverse psychology.

00:05:57.824 --> 00:06:00.035
Please, old friend, don't jump.

00:06:00.118 --> 00:06:02.871
Use another method
that won't damage your liver.

00:06:02.955 --> 00:06:05.999
Other people need it, you know.

00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:07.918
Husband, no!

00:06:08.001 --> 00:06:09.294
Out of my way, wife!

00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:11.838
I wasn't cut out to be
a bureaucrat anyway.

00:06:11.922 --> 00:06:15.175
I'm only anal 78.36% of the time.

00:06:15.259 --> 00:06:17.302
I'm not worthy to stamp a form

00:06:17.386 --> 00:06:20.514
so I'll stamp the pavement
with my flabby body.

00:06:20.597 --> 00:06:22.140
Bureaucrat Conrad,

00:06:22.224 --> 00:06:24.518
if you complete your death transaction

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:27.563
without filing a suicide
and/or falling accident permit

00:06:27.646 --> 00:06:29.815
you will be posthumously demoted.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.609
Life, death...

00:06:32.985 --> 00:06:36.405
Either way I'm demoted to a tiny cubicle.

00:06:38.073 --> 00:06:41.952
Sweet something of someplace.

00:06:42.035 --> 00:06:44.871
As your superior,
I hereby relieve you of duty.

00:06:45.122 --> 00:06:46.790
Consider yourself on paid vacation.

00:06:46.915 --> 00:06:49.668
The ultimate penalty.

00:06:49.751 --> 00:06:53.422
I recommend the health cure
on Spa 5, the sauna planet.

00:06:53.505 --> 00:06:56.425
- Here, read.
- Spa 5? Is it good?

00:06:56.508 --> 00:07:00.429
Oh, it's wonderful.
I don't know anything about it,

00:07:00.512 --> 00:07:03.473
but they give me a bucket of krill
for every patient I send.

00:07:03.557 --> 00:07:04.850
Naturally, I'll have to assign

00:07:04.933 --> 00:07:07.102
a bureaucrat to fill in for Hermes
while he's away.

00:07:07.185 --> 00:07:09.646
I assign me. I accept. Welcome aboard.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:14.318
Then it's settled. Hermes will relax
and Zoidberg will eat. Hurrah!

00:07:17.112 --> 00:07:19.323
I've been reviewing
your corporate records.

00:07:19.406 --> 00:07:20.908
Regarding last Monday's delivery,

00:07:20.991 --> 00:07:22.826
why did it take
twice as long as scheduled?

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.786
Fry got his head stuck in a crater.

00:07:24.953 --> 00:07:26.788
I thought it would fit.

00:07:27.748 --> 00:07:31.293
And during this period of head-crater
interaction, what were you doing?

00:07:31.376 --> 00:07:34.046
Martini drinking contest
with the autopilot.

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:36.757
I would have had him this time,
but we ran out of olives.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:37.841
I can explain.

00:07:37.925 --> 00:07:40.135
You really think you can explain
how you left port

00:07:40.219 --> 00:07:42.679
without a full complement of olives?
I think not.

00:07:42.763 --> 00:07:45.057
- What is this, high school?
- Locker check.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.604
Why isn't this jacket
in alphabetical order?

00:07:50.687 --> 00:07:52.064
- What?
- The zipper.

00:07:52.147 --> 00:07:53.982
It should be at the bottom.

00:07:59.321 --> 00:08:01.949
Hey, sometimes a guy gets lonely.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:11.291
I've never seen anything like this.

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:16.088
- Why is there yogurt in this cap?
- I can explain that.

00:08:16.171 --> 00:08:20.217
See, it used to be milk, and, well,
time makes fools of us all.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.969
You are all dismissed.

00:08:22.052 --> 00:08:23.554
Fry, I will speak to you alone.

00:08:28.433 --> 00:08:31.770
Uh, wait. This is the other Fry's locker.
I'm Fry with a P-H.

00:08:31.853 --> 00:08:33.939
Admit it, Fry, you're a slob.

00:08:33.964 --> 00:08:34.965
Mmm.

00:08:35.107 --> 00:08:37.401
A dirty, filthy slob.

00:08:39.444 --> 00:08:42.114
Dirty boy! Dirty, dirty, dirty!

00:08:42.197 --> 00:08:43.574
What the hell's going on?

00:08:43.657 --> 00:08:46.201
I thought you were anti-dirty,
not pro-dirty.

00:08:46.226 --> 00:08:48.353
I'm surrounded by neat freaks every day.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:52.249
There's nothing kinkier to me
than a filthy slop jock like you.

00:08:52.332 --> 00:08:53.417
Oh, stop.

00:08:55.836 --> 00:08:59.339
Now listen, you filthy pig,
no one can know about us.

00:08:59.423 --> 00:09:03.010
- If anyone asks, I'll deny it.
- Just like every other girl I've dated.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:09.725
And two, and three, and four,
and, come on, work those arms.

00:09:13.312 --> 00:09:16.106
This is no spa. It's a forced labor camp.

00:09:16.189 --> 00:09:18.984
Curse that Dr. Zoidberg.
If I get out of here,

00:09:19.067 --> 00:09:21.612
he'll be looking down
the business end of a shrimp fork.

00:09:21.695 --> 00:09:24.990
Give him one for me, too, mate.
I don't know why I go to him.

00:09:25.115 --> 00:09:27.451
I don't miss twice, campers.

00:09:30.737 --> 00:09:35.284
And for those six and a half reasons
I am demoting Leela to copilot.

00:09:35.367 --> 00:09:37.327
"Copilot"? Under who?

00:09:37.411 --> 00:09:39.496
- The autopilot.
- That drunk?

00:09:40.956 --> 00:09:43.750
Mr. Bender, you are now
in charge of coordinating

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:45.335
the professor's bodily functions.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.796
- Ahh!
- That's a full-time job.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.298
And, Fry, as for you,

00:09:49.381 --> 00:09:51.842
I am promoting you
to executive delivery boy.

00:09:51.925 --> 00:09:53.510
You will no longer go on deliveries

00:09:53.594 --> 00:09:55.804
and you will have
your own office next to mine.

00:09:55.888 --> 00:09:57.431
All right!

00:09:58.807 --> 00:10:02.603
Mr. Bender, would you high-five him
so that we can continue this meeting?

00:10:03.437 --> 00:10:05.063
And on the rebound?

00:10:05.606 --> 00:10:06.732
Ow!

00:10:06.815 --> 00:10:08.025
Meeting adjourned.

00:10:11.987 --> 00:10:14.698
I can't figure out
why she's so nice to you, Fry.

00:10:14.781 --> 00:10:16.909
She's a hateful monster, this Morgan.

00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:18.493
She scolded and hit me.

00:10:18.577 --> 00:10:22.206
I tell you, she's risking
my friendship with her.

00:10:22.289 --> 00:10:23.957
Bender! What happened to you?

00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:26.376
Morgan made me walk the professor.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:31.006
There we were in the park when suddenly,
some old lady says I stole her purse.

00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:32.674
I chucked the professor at her

00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:36.303
but she kept coming, so I had to hit her
with this purse I found.

00:10:36.386 --> 00:10:38.931
The point is, it's Morgan's fault.

00:10:39.014 --> 00:10:41.016
That pencil-pushing scaz-wag.

00:10:41.099 --> 00:10:43.352
Why, if she were here, I'd...

00:10:43.435 --> 00:10:44.978
Is she behind me?

00:10:45.062 --> 00:10:46.897
No, I'm in front of you.

00:10:52.319 --> 00:10:54.571
Morgan? It's 3:00 a.m.

00:10:54.655 --> 00:10:56.990
I know. A skunk knocked over my garbage

00:10:57.074 --> 00:10:59.243
and suddenly,
all I could think of was you.

00:11:03.372 --> 00:11:08.502
My God. It's so repulsive.

00:11:09.002 --> 00:11:11.505
So, this is where you eat?

00:11:11.588 --> 00:11:13.590
Eat and sleep.

00:11:14.341 --> 00:11:15.551
Oh, Fry!

00:11:17.594 --> 00:11:20.597
Uh, wait! Bender's my roommate.
He could be back any second.

00:11:20.681 --> 00:11:24.059
Not likely. I ordered him to flush out
the professor's ear wax.

00:11:27.479 --> 00:11:30.190
Hey, Fry, I made you a candle with...

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.817
What the...

00:11:33.986 --> 00:11:38.448
Oh, now I see. Now I get it.

00:11:38.532 --> 00:11:40.826
Now the pieces are falling into place.

00:11:40.909 --> 00:11:42.744
The office, the promotion,

00:11:42.828 --> 00:11:45.831
that dwarf in my book club
who steals my opinions.

00:11:45.914 --> 00:11:47.833
It's all coming together now.

00:11:48.208 --> 00:11:51.670
I must say this opens my eyes.

00:11:51.753 --> 00:11:54.756
Another case closed, my dear Watson.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.134
Morgan, come back. He's stuck in a loop.

00:11:57.217 --> 00:12:00.596
For I was blind but now I see.

00:12:00.929 --> 00:12:03.098
The cat's out of the bag now.

00:12:03.182 --> 00:12:07.394
Mr. Bender, about last night,
that was just a misunderstanding.

00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:10.105
You didn't understand?
Well, let me explain.

00:12:10.189 --> 00:12:12.566
You were having sex with you.

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:16.320
No, you see, a bureaucrat of my rank
isn't supposed to fraternize.

00:12:16.403 --> 00:12:18.530
That's what makes it so juicy.

00:12:18.614 --> 00:12:21.575
It's a forbidden fruit angle
everybody loves.

00:12:21.658 --> 00:12:25.287
First I'll say, "You'll never guess
who saw Fry and Morgan doing it."

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:26.955
And they'll say, "Who, Bender, who?"

00:12:27.039 --> 00:12:32.628
And I'll say, "It was lovable old Bender."

00:12:32.711 --> 00:12:35.923
- Hey, what did you do to him?
- I downloaded his brain.

00:12:36.006 --> 00:12:37.841
Everything that is Bender is right here.

00:12:37.925 --> 00:12:41.345
His mind, his memories...
His in-your-face interface.

00:12:41.428 --> 00:12:44.515
I am Bender. Please insert girder.

00:12:44.598 --> 00:12:48.602
But, Bender need brain for smart making.

00:12:50.979 --> 00:12:53.732
What did you do now? Stop doing things.

00:12:53.815 --> 00:12:56.610
I sent the disk to be filed
at the Central Bureaucracy.

00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:59.530
I did what I had to do, Fry.
He was a bad robot.

00:12:59.613 --> 00:13:02.908
No, he was a bad friend.
I want him back right now.

00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:05.702
Then you should have filed
a request 20 years ago.

00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:08.914
Grr! I'm sick of you and your bureaucracy.

00:13:11.542 --> 00:13:12.835
Dirty boy!

00:13:12.918 --> 00:13:14.211
Dirty boy!

00:13:19.449 --> 00:13:21.660
You and Morgan were having an affair?

00:13:21.743 --> 00:13:22.744
I couldn't help it.

00:13:22.828 --> 00:13:25.122
She loved me because of the part of me
that's a slob.

00:13:25.205 --> 00:13:27.624
I loved her because of the part of me
that's desperate.

00:13:27.708 --> 00:13:31.086
I am Bender. Please insert girder.

00:13:31.169 --> 00:13:32.295
Poor Bender.

00:13:32.379 --> 00:13:35.048
Without his brain
he's become all quiet and helpful.

00:13:35.132 --> 00:13:38.385
We've got to go to the Central Bureaucracy
and get that disk back.

00:13:38.468 --> 00:13:40.762
- Yes, we must.
- Yeah.

00:13:40.846 --> 00:13:42.639
Why?

00:13:43.515 --> 00:13:46.184
Well, those arguments aside,
we're still going.

00:13:46.268 --> 00:13:49.396
You can't just waltz into
the Central Bureaucracy.

00:13:49.479 --> 00:13:52.816
It's a tangled web of red tape
and regulations.

00:13:52.899 --> 00:13:55.986
I've never been,
but a friend of mine went completely mad

00:13:56.069 --> 00:13:58.030
just trying to find the washroom there.

00:13:58.113 --> 00:14:00.824
Then we'll need a guide.
Someone who's been there before.

00:14:00.907 --> 00:14:03.910
I've been there. Lots of times.

00:14:09.624 --> 00:14:13.045
Look at that. The carts go out full,
but they come in empty.

00:14:13.128 --> 00:14:15.672
- It's criminally inefficient.
- Quiet, mate.

00:14:15.756 --> 00:14:19.176
Pulling the empty carts is
the closest thing we get to sleep.

00:14:19.259 --> 00:14:20.260
But don't ya see?

00:14:20.344 --> 00:14:23.680
They could increase efficiency 4%
if they used the empty carts

00:14:23.764 --> 00:14:25.432
to bring in heavy mining machinery.

00:14:25.515 --> 00:14:27.976
Hey, I like the way you think.

00:14:31.271 --> 00:14:32.439
Oh, Lord.

00:14:33.648 --> 00:14:36.860
You know, you ought to be
a bureaucrat or something.

00:14:45.952 --> 00:14:47.746
Man, how long is this going to take?

00:14:47.829 --> 00:14:49.873
I'm still waiting on my birth certificate.

00:14:49.956 --> 00:14:53.168
Well, it doesn't look like
I'll make it inside with the rest of you.

00:14:53.251 --> 00:14:56.004
But good luck. Just leave me where I drop.

00:14:57.881 --> 00:15:00.008
Oh, great. Someone had a baby.

00:15:00.092 --> 00:15:02.177
Come on. I have a better idea.

00:15:02.761 --> 00:15:06.264
Excuse me. We're from
the Planet Express delivery company.

00:15:06.348 --> 00:15:07.974
We're here to deliver a robot.

00:15:08.058 --> 00:15:09.309
I am Bender.

00:15:09.393 --> 00:15:11.395
Please insert girder.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.439
Looks like we've got a new office cutup.

00:15:25.617 --> 00:15:27.452
Look out!

00:15:27.577 --> 00:15:31.248
I'm going to crash my slow-mobile.
I had to swerve to avoid you.

00:15:31.331 --> 00:15:34.960
While you're crashing could you tell us
where all these canisters end up?

00:15:35.043 --> 00:15:36.962
Oh, you want Central Filing.

00:15:37.045 --> 00:15:38.130
- Okay.
- Thank you.

00:15:38.213 --> 00:15:39.464
- Thanks.
- Wonderful.

00:15:40.132 --> 00:15:42.050
No!

00:15:45.087 --> 00:15:47.297
Central Filing?
Of course I know where that is.

00:15:47.381 --> 00:15:49.091
- I'm a Grade 20.
- Where is it?

00:15:49.174 --> 00:15:52.844
- I can't tell you. What do I look like?
- A Grade 16?

00:15:52.928 --> 00:15:55.806
We're getting nowhere slowly.

00:15:55.889 --> 00:15:58.642
Here. I'll address this
to the Central Filing room.

00:15:58.725 --> 00:16:02.646
Then we'll track it
with my wrist LoJack-a-mater.

00:16:02.729 --> 00:16:03.939
Cold.

00:16:04.064 --> 00:16:05.107
Warmer.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.317
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot.

00:16:27.504 --> 00:16:30.299
Please don't tell my supervisor
I was sleeping.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:37.180
This is it. We'll just run in,
grab Bender's disk, and run out. Got it?

00:16:48.108 --> 00:16:50.360
We'll never find that disk,
will we, Bender?

00:16:50.444 --> 00:16:53.614
I am Bender. Please insert girder.

00:16:53.697 --> 00:16:57.409
You're right. Nothing is over
as long as there's one thin ray of hope.

00:16:57.492 --> 00:16:58.660
Lost something?

00:16:58.744 --> 00:17:02.497
I should have known you'd come here
rather than follow proper procedure.

00:17:02.581 --> 00:17:05.334
And I did know,
and that's why I came here.

00:17:05.417 --> 00:17:07.085
Listen, Morgan, we're through.

00:17:07.169 --> 00:17:10.255
You're an evil, heartless woman
and I never want to see you again.

00:17:10.339 --> 00:17:13.008
However, would you help us get Bender back
for old times' sake?

00:17:13.091 --> 00:17:16.428
I'm afraid he's lost
in the master in-pile.

00:17:16.511 --> 00:17:18.138
And it would take some sort of giant

00:17:18.221 --> 00:17:21.058
mechanical atomic-powered
sorting machine to find him.

00:17:21.141 --> 00:17:22.392
You rang?

00:17:24.394 --> 00:17:28.482
Damn it, Hermes, just jump already.
Stop hogging that healthy liver.

00:17:28.565 --> 00:17:30.400
No, I want to live.

00:17:30.484 --> 00:17:35.030
Organizing that forced-labor spa
rekindled my lifelong love of Bureaucracy.

00:17:35.113 --> 00:17:38.659
My Hermes got that hellhole
running so efficiently

00:17:38.742 --> 00:17:43.413
that all the physical labor is now done
by a single Australian man.

00:17:43.497 --> 00:17:45.040
But how did you know we were here?

00:17:45.123 --> 00:17:46.541
Dr. Zoidberg brought us.

00:17:46.625 --> 00:17:49.711
It was me. I'm the hero.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.218
Request for explanation
of incident meeting.

00:17:59.262 --> 00:18:02.557
- Number one point zero.
- Number one point zero.

00:18:02.641 --> 00:18:03.976
I hereby petition you

00:18:04.059 --> 00:18:07.229
for an emergency sort-and-file
under regulation two-point...

00:18:07.312 --> 00:18:10.732
Don't quote me regulations.

00:18:10.816 --> 00:18:13.777
I co-chaired the committee
that reviewed the recommendation

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.197
to revise the color of the book
that regulation's in.

00:18:17.281 --> 00:18:19.157
We kept it gray.

00:18:19.241 --> 00:18:23.203
Sir, please. I must locate the disk
with my friend's brain on it.

00:18:23.287 --> 00:18:27.457
Very well. But your bureaucratic license
will be revoked

00:18:27.541 --> 00:18:31.461
if you fail to sort the master in-pile
by closing time.

00:18:31.545 --> 00:18:32.879
1:00 p.m.

00:18:33.922 --> 00:18:35.882
That's only four minutes from now.

00:18:36.216 --> 00:18:38.093
Requisition me a beat.

00:18:47.769 --> 00:18:50.814
When I was four there was
A hurricane in Kingston town

00:18:50.897 --> 00:18:52.816
With a foot and a half of water

00:18:53.275 --> 00:18:55.777
Everyone was all right,
But I cried all night

00:18:55.861 --> 00:18:58.155
It blew my alphabet blocks out of order

00:18:58.238 --> 00:19:01.450
And they said this boy's born
To be a bureaucrat

00:19:01.533 --> 00:19:03.744
Born to be all obsessive and snotty

00:19:03.827 --> 00:19:05.454
I made my friends and relations

00:19:05.537 --> 00:19:06.872
File long applications

00:19:06.955 --> 00:19:08.999
To get into my tenth birthday party

00:19:09.082 --> 00:19:12.210
But something changed
When my man turned pro

00:19:12.294 --> 00:19:14.504
I was sorting but I wasn't smiling

00:19:14.588 --> 00:19:17.341
He forgot that it's not
About badges and ranks

00:19:17.424 --> 00:19:19.801
It's supposed to be about the filing

00:19:19.885 --> 00:19:20.886
People

00:19:20.969 --> 00:19:22.554
We didn't choose to be bureaucrats

00:19:22.638 --> 00:19:25.432
No, that's what almighty Jah made us

00:19:25.515 --> 00:19:28.060
We'd treat people like swine
And make 'em stand in line

00:19:28.143 --> 00:19:30.228
Even if nobody paid us

00:19:30.312 --> 00:19:33.357
They say the world looks down
On the bureaucrats

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.109
They say we're anal compulsive and weird

00:19:36.193 --> 00:19:38.820
But when push comes to shove
You've got to do what you love

00:19:38.904 --> 00:19:40.822
Even if it's not a good idea

00:19:40.906 --> 00:19:41.907
Zoidberg!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.076
They said I probably
Shouldn't be a surgeon

00:19:44.159 --> 00:19:46.703
They pooh-poohed my electric frankfurter

00:19:46.787 --> 00:19:49.623
They said I probably
Shouldn't fly with just one eye

00:19:49.706 --> 00:19:52.125
I am Bender
Please insert girder

00:19:54.336 --> 00:19:55.754
Everybody sing Jamaica

00:19:55.837 --> 00:19:56.964
Jamaica

00:19:57.047 --> 00:19:59.174
Just the bureaucrats
Jamaica

00:19:59.257 --> 00:20:01.093
Just the Grade 19s

00:20:01.176 --> 00:20:02.344
Jamaica

00:20:02.427 --> 00:20:03.428
Sing me home

00:20:03.512 --> 00:20:05.847
When push comes to shove
You've got to do what you love

00:20:05.931 --> 00:20:07.641
Even if it's not a good idea

00:20:10.185 --> 00:20:11.853
I'm Bender, baby!

00:20:11.937 --> 00:20:13.855
Please insert liquor!

00:20:15.148 --> 00:20:16.858
- Congratulations.
- Way to go.

00:20:16.942 --> 00:20:18.277
Congratulations indeed.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.238
But you finished with two seconds to spare
so I'm demoting you.

00:20:21.321 --> 00:20:23.490
A good bureaucrat never finishes early.

00:20:24.241 --> 00:20:27.160
That's okay, Hermes.
At least we have you back.

00:20:27.244 --> 00:20:28.370
Not yet, you don't.

00:20:28.453 --> 00:20:30.998
I'm still acting bureaucrat
of Planet Express

00:20:31.081 --> 00:20:32.874
and I have some changes to make.

00:20:32.958 --> 00:20:35.711
First, Fry, you're fired. Second...

00:20:35.794 --> 00:20:36.837
Not so fast.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.005
While I was sorting

00:20:38.088 --> 00:20:41.508
I came upon a certain document
filed by one Morgan Proctor.

00:20:41.591 --> 00:20:42.718
Form "B."

00:20:42.801 --> 00:20:45.887
Notification of romantic entanglement.

00:20:45.971 --> 00:20:47.848
That's right. She fraternized me.

00:20:47.931 --> 00:20:51.935
That form isn't about you.
It refers to my high school prom date.

00:20:52.019 --> 00:20:55.188
It was a regulation date that ended
in regulation disappointment.

00:20:55.272 --> 00:20:58.525
Yes, but you only stamped it four times.

00:21:00.444 --> 00:21:03.572
No, no. I was young and reckless.

00:21:03.655 --> 00:21:06.617
Bureaucrat Conrad,
you are technically correct.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.452
The best kind of correct.

00:21:08.535 --> 00:21:11.413
I hereby promote you to Grade 37.

00:21:12.623 --> 00:21:15.000
And as for you. Guards.

00:21:16.043 --> 00:21:19.421
Bring me the forms
I need to fill out to have her taken away.

00:21:21.715 --> 00:21:25.427
Well, it looks like I'll be needing
my heroic bureaucrat back.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.763
At severely reduced pay, of course.

00:21:29.139 --> 00:21:30.807
It's better than nothing.

00:21:30.891 --> 00:21:33.393
What about me? Can I come back
at severely reduced pay?

00:21:33.477 --> 00:21:37.940
You got it, mon.
In fact, severely reduced pay all around.

00:21:41.568 --> 00:21:44.321
Come on, wife. Let's blow this joint.

00:21:46.198 --> 00:21:48.200
Now it's time for my song.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.495
When I was two
There was a tidal wave in...

00:21:51.954 --> 00:21:52.955
Aw...